PATCH 645: one full CPU and resident guest RAM owner for1280/23c4/133a.

Original device_start_prefix_case proves actual1280 full GP/segments/raw and
lazy flags/control fields, caller77ee frame and DWORD guest RET. The source
TCB is a raw logicalf0010000 operand; DS addition wraps to linear10000, then
paging resolves it. It is not a port host pointer. Restore the actual sorted
entry using FistCpuState; delete the obsolete two-lane carrier rather than
padding missing registers. Every MOV preserves flags/untouched bits and
uses original WORD/DWORD widths. Each original fetch uses the shared clock.

Use one explicit resident-RAM resolver for the original guest segments,
CR3 and PDE/PTE frame fields. Apply it to the already-restored23c4 table,
133a configuration reads and shared nearRET too. Original paging.cpp and
paging.h define four-KiB resident page translation. Accessed/dirty/writable
pages are proved by the captured input. Cold/fault/MMIO/privilege paths and
legacy flattened production memory remain unintegrated, and fail rather
than receiving guessed mappings or safe values. No separate RAM state,
fixed physical module base or guest pointer constant is introduced.

The reaching tests now run complete original16MiB physical RAM with all37
CPU words, without address normalization. Actual default/control inputs,
every config/dispatch/reset fetch and actual caller RET are compared on
both targets. Controlled source words reproduce the accepted width case;
full RAM is restored before the original caller resumes. Nine-frame state
sequences retain the actual caller fetch; thin budgets use original PIC.
Production77e2/op6c, post-reset ORb, bank/device/IRQ/IRET/IF, first817 and
final mixedPCM/complete original output acceptance remain open.
